llowing timeline and fees:)/K[9]/P 119 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/H3/T(2.2. The Accreditation Process There are three stages in the process, with the following timeline and fees:)/Type/StructElem>>endobj851 0 obj<</K[1581 0 R]/P 119 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/L/Type/StructElem>>endobj852 0 obj<</K[1582 0 R]/P 119 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/L/Type/StructElem>>endobj853 0 obj<</K[1583 0 R]/P 119 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/L/Type/StructElem>>endobj275 0 obj<</E(Fees: For full details, including any circumstance where additional fees may become due \(e.g. cancellation of a pre-arranged inspection\), please see the Finance Policy in Appendix B of this Handbook.)/K[15]/P 119 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/H3/T(Fees: For full details, including any circumstance where additional fees may become due \(e.g. cancellation of a pre-arranged inspection\), please see the Finance Policy in Appendix B of this Handbook.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj276 0 obj<</E(Timeline: The process is designed to be as unobtrusive to an institution's daily operation as possible. If the information submitted to us during Stage 1 is complete and an institution is immediately available for inspection at Stages 2 and 3, the entire \process can take as little as eight weeks to complete. The number of weeks at each stage given above is the average period of time we find institutions take to get through the process, factoring in arranging dates for inspection. We find that there are tw\o main reasons it can take longer:)/K[16]/P 119 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/H3/T(Timeline: The process is designed to be as unobtrusive to an institution's daily operation as possible. If the information submitted to us during Stage 1 is complete and an institution is immediately available for inspection at Stages 2 and 3, the entire \process can take as little as eight weeks to complete. The number of weeks at each stage given above is the average period of time we find institutions take to get through the process, factoring in arranging dates for inspection. We find that there are tw\o main reasons it can take longer:)/Type/StructElem>>endobj854 0 obj<</K[1584 0 R 1585 0 R]/P 119 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/L/Type/StructElem>>endobj281 0 obj<</A[917 0 R 0]/K[21]/P 119 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj278 0 obj<</A[915 0 R 0]/K[18]/P 119 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj282 0 obj<</A[918 0 R 0]/K[22]/P 119 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj277 0 obj<</E(*Note, in some circumstances the process may differ, and, in such cases, the Annual Fee will be due from the initial award of Accreditation.)/K[17]/P 119 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj918 0 obj<</BBox[79.39379 43.13313 492.98248 43.88313]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj915 0 obj<</BBox[-15.918079 57.137573 591.81085 140.41895]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj917 0 obj<</BBox[169.42862 -360.5492 754.3202 212.5249]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj1584 0 obj<</K[913 0 R]/P 854 0 R/S/LI/Type/StructElem>>endobj1585 0 obj<</K[914 0 R]/P 854 0 R/S/LI/Type/StructElem>>endobj914 0 obj<</K 274 0 R/P 1585 0 R/S/LBody/Type/StructElem>>endobj274 0 obj<</E(The institution does not follow the process. E.g. submission of incomplete information, non-payment of fees, unavailability of dates for inspection, or simply failing to respond to ASIC communication. We recommend that institutions assign a designated con\tact person to deal with ASIC correspondence regarding the process.)/K[14]/P 914 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/H3/T(The institution does not follow the process. E.g. submission of incomplete information, non-payment of fees, unavailability of dates for inspection, or simply failing to respond to ASIC communication. We recommend that institutions assign a designated con\tact person to deal with ASIC correspondence regarding the process.)/Type/StructElem>>endobj913 0 obj<</K 273 0 R/P 1584 0 R/S/LBody/Type/StructElem>>endobj273 0 obj<</E(There is an extended period between the award of Interim Accreditation and the Stage 3 inspection taking place \(usually the case for newly operating institutions and can be no longer than 12 months\). )/K[13]/P 913 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/H3/T(There is an extended period between the award of Interim Accreditation and the Stage 3 inspection taking place \(usually the case for newly operating institutions and can be no longer than 12 months\). )/Type/StructElem>>endobj1583 0 obj<</K[912 0 R]/P 853 0 R/S/LI/Type/StructElem>>endobj912 0 obj<</K 272 0 R/P 1583 0 R/S/LBody/Type/StructElem>>endobj272 0 obj<</E(Stage 3: Inspection. 6-8 weeks. The Stage 3 Inspection Fee is due before the visit is confirmed. If the AAC grants Accreditation \(again, following the visit, Report, and Decision\), subsequent Annual Fees continue to be payable on the same date each year\ as the Initial Annual Accreditation Fee* \(at the award of Interim\).)/K[12]/P 912 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/H3/T(Stage 3: Inspection. 6-8 weeks. The Stage 3 Inspection Fee is due before the visit is confirmed. If the AAC grants Accreditation \(again, following the visit, Report, and Decision\), subsequent Annual Fees continue to be payable on the same date each year\ as the Initial Annual Accreditation Fee* \(at the award of Interim\).)/Type/StructElem>>endobj1582 0 obj<</K[911 0 R]/P 852 0 R/S/LI/Type/StructElem>>endobj911 0 obj<</K 271 0 R/P 1582 0 R/S/LBody/Type/StructElem>>endobj271 0 obj<</E(Stage 2: Inspection. 6-8 weeks. If the AAC awards Interim Accreditation \(following the visit, Report, and Decision\), the Initial Annual Accreditation Fee becomes payable. )/K[11]/P 911 0 R/Pg 14 0 R/S/H3/T(Stage 2: Inspection. 6-8 weeks. If the AAC awards Interim Accreditation \(following the visit, Report, and Decision\), the Initial Annual Accreditation Fee becomes payable. )/Type/StructElem>>endobj1581 0 obj<</K[910 0 R]/P 851 0 R/S/LI/Type/StructElem>>endobj910 0 obj<</K 270 0 R/P 1581 0 R/S/LBody/Type/StructElem>>endobj270 0 obj<</E(Stage 1: Application and Review. 1-2 weeks. Stage 1 and 2 Fees due wi