it]/Next 2288 0 R/Parent 2176 0 R/Title(UK BASED. INTERNATIONAL FOCUS.)>>endobj2288 0 obj<</Dest[11 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2176 0 R/Prev 2287 0 R/Title(CONTENTS)>>endobj2000 0 obj<</Dest[10 0 R/Fit]/Next 2176 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 1689 0 R/Title(and governments to improve the)>>endobj1689 0 obj<</Dest[10 0 R/Fit]/Next 2000 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 1060 0 R/Title(We work globally with institutions)>>endobj1060 0 obj<</Count -1/Dest[9 0 R/Fit]/First 1688 0 R/Last 1688 0 R/Next 1689 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 600 0 R/Title(Handbook)>>endobj1688 0 obj<</Dest[9 0 R/Fit]/Parent 1060 0 R/Title(For Quality International Education.)>>endobj600 0 obj<</Dest[9 0 R/Fit]/Next 1060 0 R/Parent 7 0 R/Prev 35 0 R/Title(Accreditation)>>endobj2335 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Next 2340 0 R/Parent 2330 0 R/Title(UK Government approved ASIC is a UK Visas and Immigration \(part of the UK Government Home Office\) approved accreditation body for the Short-Term Study and Standard Visitor visas.)>>endobj2336 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2330 0 R/Prev 2341 0 R/Title(Please see our website for the full list: www.asic.org.uk)>>endobj2334 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Next 2330 0 R/Parent 2327 0 R/Prev 2333 0 R/Title(Grow your international reputation and recruitment with ASIC Accreditation.)>>endobj2333 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Next 2334 0 R/Parent 2327 0 R/Prev 2329 0 R/Title(15 16)>>endobj2341 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Next 2336 0 R/Parent 2330 0 R/Prev 2340 0 R/Title(ISO 9001:2015 Accredited  ASIC holds ISO 9001:2015 certification in recognition of our commitment to high standards in the accreditation process and internal procedures.)>>endobj2340 0 obj<</Dest[12 0 R/Fit]/Next 2341 0 R/Parent 2330 0 R/Prev 2335 0 R/Title(INQAAHE: The International Network for Quality Assurance Agencies in Higher Education INQAAHE is a worldwide association of organisations that is active in the theory and practice of quality assurance \(QA\) in higher education \(HE\). ASIC is a Full Memb\er of INQAAHE. Approved Members are independently assessed and approved by the Membership & Membership Services Committee of the INQAAHE Board.)>>endobj2345 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2349 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Title(ASIC inspects the full range of provision and supporting activities offered by an institution, together with a detailed consideration of its documentation, helping to ensure a satisfactory level of operation is maintained.)>>endobj2346 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2350 0 R/Title(The institution does not follow the process. E.g. submission of incomplete information, non-payment of fees, unavailability of dates for inspection, or simply failing to respond to ASIC communication. We recommend that institutions assign a designated con\tact person to deal with ASIC correspondence regarding the process.)>>endobj2350 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2346 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2354 0 R/Title(There is an extended period between the award of Interim Accreditation and the Stage 3 inspection taking place \(usually the case for newly operating institutions and can be no longer than 12 months\).)>>endobj2354 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2350 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2358 0 R/Title(Timeline: The process is designed to be as unobtrusive to an institution's daily operation as possible. If the information submitted to us during Stage 1 is complete and an institution is immediately available for inspection at Stages 2 and 3, the entire \process can take as little as eight weeks to complete. The number of weeks at each stage given above is the average period of time we find institutions take to get through the process, factoring in arranging dates for inspection. We find that there are tw\o main reasons it can take longer:)>>endobj2358 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2354 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2362 0 R/Title(Fees: For full details, including any circumstance where additional fees may become due \(e.g. cancellation of a pre-arranged inspection\), please see the Finance Policy in Appendix B of this Handbook.)>>endobj2362 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2358 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2366 0 R/Title(Stage 3: Inspection. 6-8 weeks. The Stage 3 Inspection Fee is due before the visit is confirmed. If the AAC grants Accreditation \(again, following the visit, Report, and Decision\), subsequent Annual Fees continue to be payable on the same date each year\ as the Initial Annual Accreditation Fee* \(at the award of Interim\).)>>endobj2366 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2362 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2370 0 R/Title(Stage 2: Inspection. 6-8 weeks. If the AAC awards Interim Accreditation \(following the visit, Report, and Decision\), the Initial Annual Accreditation Fee becomes payable.)>>endobj2370 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2366 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2373 0 R/Title(Stage 1: Application and Review. 1-2 weeks. Stage 1 and 2 Fees due with Application submission.)>>endobj2373 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2370 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2369 0 R/Title(2.2. The Accreditation Process There are three stages in the process, with the following timeline and fees:)>>endobj2369 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2373 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2365 0 R/Title(updated background checks.)>>endobj2365 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2369 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2361 0 R/Title(evidence arising from the consideration of complaints and appeals;)>>endobj2361 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2365 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2357 0 R/Title(evidence provided by official agencies;)>>endobj2357 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2361 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2353 0 R/Title(documentation provided by the institution;)>>endobj2353 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2357 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2349 0 R/Title(the Report submitted by the Reporting Inspector\(s\) after an inspection visit;)>>endobj2349 0 obj<</Dest[14 0 R/Fit]/Next 2353 0 R/Parent 2342 0 R/Prev 2345 0 R/Title(2.1. The ASIC Accreditation Committee \(AAC\) The AAC are responsible for making all decisions regarding the award, maintenance, and withdrawal or suspension of Accreditation. Please note that no member of ASIC staff is able to indicate, deliver, or overr\ide any decision that is made by the Committee. The AAC make decisions based on the following evidence:)>>endobj2395 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2389 0 R/Parent 2385 0 R/Prev 2402 0 R/Title(During the visit, the Inspector\(s\) will meet with the Owner\(s\)* to discuss the institution's Business Plan for ongoing operation and development; the Inspector will also discuss the format and arrangements for the Stage 3 visit.)>>endobj2402 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2395 0 R/Parent 2385 0 R/Prev 2411 0 R/Title(Inspection Overview: Stage 2 focuses on statutory and immigration requirements, premises and health and safety, management, adequacy of teaching resources for the advertised/planned courses, and staff and student records.)>>endobj2411 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2402 0 R/Parent 2385 0 R/Prev 2401 0 R/Title(Asking for an organogram.)>>endobj2401 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2411 0 R/Parent 2385 0 R/Prev 2394 0 R/Title(Explaining how the documentation needs to be presented in the room in the order of the ASIC Areas of Operation: A, B, C etc.)>>endobj2394 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2401 0 R/Parent 2385 0 R/Prev 2388 0 R/Title(Clarifying the requirements for a suitable   room for the inspectors to use.)>>endobj2404 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2397 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2413 0 R/Title(Please note, ASIC expects institutions to tell staff and students about the visit, making them aware of the likelihood of lesson observations and that they may receive a request to meet with the Inspector\(s\).)>>endobj2413 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2404 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2421 0 R/Title(During the visit, the Inspector\(s\) will hold meetings with the senior management team, administration and teaching staff \(without management present\) and with a group/groups of students \(without staff present\). Teaching and lesson observation will o\ccur, along with the inspection of learning resources, student/staff refreshment facilities, and any accommodation owned by the institution. [1])>>endobj2421 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2413 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2429 0 R/Title(Format: This varies in relation to the institution's size, nature, location, and complexity of provision. The visit is usually one day for smaller providers, and larger institutions \(more than 1000 Full-Time Equivalent students \(FTEs\) with an extensive\ academic programme\) may require two days. The number of visiting inspectors will also depend on the above criteria.)>>endobj2429 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2421 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2436 0 R/Title(Overview: Stage 3 will evaluate criteria from all eight Areas of Operation \(see "ASIC UK Standards for Accreditation"\) with particular emphasis on academic matters, including teaching and learning, resources and quality management, student welfare, and \reporting to official bodies. The Inspector\(s\) will also evaluate whether the institution has resolved the issues \(if any\) identified during Stage 2. To assist with further development, the Inspector will encourage institutions to look for ways in whi\ch they might continue to improve their provision and provide recommendations to help achieve this.)>>endobj2436 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2429 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2442 0 R/Title(2.2.3. Stage 3 Pre-inspection: The ASIC Office will arrange inspection dates and send the "Stage 3 Checklist of Documents." Again as above, once an inspection date is confirmed, the Lead Inspector will arrange a short remote meeting.)>>endobj2442 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2436 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2446 0 R/Title(Refuse Accreditation on the grounds that there are serious shortcomings in provision. In this case, the institution has the Right of Appeal \(Section 7\).)>>endobj2446 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2442 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2450 0 R/Title(Defer the Decision as it is perceived that there are some weaknesses in provision. ASIC will notify the institution of the conditions to satisfy and will \(usually\) give a three-month period for these to be fulfilled; when met, the institution will submi\t its evidence. [1] The AAC will meet to decide on the award of Interim.)>>endobj2450 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2446 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2453 0 R/Title(Award Interim Accreditation for a total period not exceeding 12 months \(during which the Stage 3 Inspection must occur\). The initial Annual Accreditation Fee \(Appendix B\) will become due. At this stage, the institution may then proceed straight to Sta\ge 3.)>>endobj2453 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2450 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2449 0 R/Title(Decision: The ACC will consider the evidence and determine one of the following outcomes:)>>endobj2449 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2453 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2445 0 R/Title(Confirm all "Stage 2 Checklist" documents are statisfactory)>>endobj2445 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2449 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2441 0 R/Title(Inspect administration systems and process)>>endobj2441 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2445 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2435 0 R/Title(Visit student common/refreshment areas and any institution-owned accommodation)>>endobj2435 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2441 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2428 0 R/Title(Assess classroom facilities, laboratories, and audio-visual equipment \(where applicable\))>>endobj2428 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2435 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2420 0 R/Title(Evaluate IT provision for staff and students)>>endobj2420 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2428 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2412 0 R/Title(Survey the library \(where appropriate\))>>endobj2412 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2420 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2403 0 R/Title(Examine health and safety arrangements and fire-risk related records)>>endobj2403 0 obj<</Dest[16 0 R/Fit]/Next 2412 0 R/Parent 2390 0 R/Prev 2396 0 R/Title(Undertake a tour of the premises)>>endobj2415 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2406 0 R/Parent 2398 0 R/Prev 2423 0 R/Title(Explaining that documentation needs to be presented in the room in the order of the ASIC Areas of Operation: A, B, C etc.)>>endobj2423 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2415 0 R/Parent 2398 0 R/Prev 2430 0 R/Title(Clarifying the requirements for a suitable room for the inspectors to use during the inspection.)>>endobj2430 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2423 0 R/Parent 2398 0 R/Prev 2422 0 R/Title(Reminding the institution that groups of students must also be available to meet the inspector\(s\) without members of staff.)>>endobj2422 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2430 0 R/Parent 2398 0 R/Prev 2414 0 R/Title(Highlighting that the institution will need to identify the teaching and administration staff available to meet with the Inspector\(s\).)>>endobj2414 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2422 0 R/Parent 2398 0 R/Prev 2405 0 R/Title(Asking the institution to identify which lessons will be delivered during the inspection period and provide a timetable.)>>endobj2425 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2417 0 R/Parent 2407 0 R/Prev 2432 0 R/Title(confirm all mandatory documentation** is present, adhered to, and meets requirements \(all documentation from the Stage 2 and 3 "Checklist of Documents" must be available for the Inspector to view\);)>>endobj2432 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2425 0 R/Parent 2407 0 R/Prev 2438 0 R/Title(inspect the administration systems;)>>endobj2438 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2432 0 R/Parent 2407 0 R/Prev 2437 0 R/Title(meet 1-2 representative groups of students \(depending on the number of FTEs\) - without any staff present;)>>endobj2437 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2438 0 R/Parent 2407 0 R/Prev 2431 0 R/Title(observe several teaching sessions;)>>endobj2431 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2437 0 R/Parent 2407 0 R/Prev 2424 0 R/Title(meet course/subject leaders \(if applicable\);)>>endobj2424 0 obj<</Dest[17 0 R/Fit]/Next 2431 0 R/Parent 2407 0 R/Prev 2416 0 R/Title(meet a representative group of administration and teaching staff - without any senior management present;)>>endobj2467 0 obj<</Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Next 2471 0 R/Parent 2464 0 R/Title(As with all partnerships, both sides must fulfil the necessary conditions to maintain a successful working relationship. The following sections detail ASIC's service commitments and the ongoing requirements the institution must meet to maintain Accreditat\ion.)>>endobj2468 0 obj<</Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2464 0 R/Prev 2472 0 R/Title(Institutions will also receive a Marketing Pack with the Logo, Authorised Wording, and ASIC Brand Guidelines, containing useful ideas on how to use the Logo across their promotional activities to help them get the most out of their accredited status in th\eir student recruitment and marketing activities.)>>endobj2472 0 obj<</Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Next 2468 0 R/Parent 2464 0 R/Prev 2476 0 R/Title(Following them will help providers use the resources provided with confidence.)>>endobj2476 0 obj<</Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Next 2472 0 R/Parent 2464 0 R/Prev 2479 0 R/Title(In using the Badge and Wording, the institution agrees to follow the ASIC Brand Guidelines \(and any README files sent with the resources\).)>>endobj2479 0 obj<</Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Next 2476 0 R/Parent 2464 0 R/Prev 2475 0 R/Title(If the institution chooses to discontinue its relationship with ASIC or has its award of Accreditation withdrawn by the AAC, it may no longer use the Badge/Wording; the institution must remove them from its website and promotional materials with immediate\ effect.)>>endobj2475 0 obj<</Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Next 2479 0 R/Parent 2464 0 R/Prev 2471 0 R/Title(3.1.2. Use of the ASIC Badge of Accreditation The ASIC Accreditation Logo and Authorised Wording \(along with the ASIC Brand Guidelines\) are for institutions to use in student recruitment and marketing activities. Different logos are supplied for Interim\ Accreditation and full Accreditation.)>>endobj2471 0 obj<</Dest[20 0 R/Fit]/Next 2475 0 R/Parent 2464 0 R/Prev 2467 0 R/Title(3.1. ASIC Service Commitments 3.1.1. ASIC UK Directory listing and Institution Profile on the ASIC website The online Directory entry includes the provider's address, website, and contact details to help students and other stakeholders to find the institu\tion when searching for an accredited provider/confirm the accreditation status of the institution. The additional Institution Profile area is designed to encourage those who discover the institution through the ASIC listing to contact the institution or \navigate to its website to learn more.)>>endobj2409 0 obj<</Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Next 2410 0 R/Parent 2400 0 R/Title(Note - Inappropriate complaints:)>>endobj2410 0 obj<</Dest[24 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2400 0 R/Prev 2409 0 R/Title(4.2.1. ASIC and Institution action:)>>endobj2393 0 obj<</Dest[25 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2387 0 R/Title(Note that ASIC reserves the right to remove Accreditation without Appeal in specific cases, e.g. ASIC will withdraw the Right of Appeal if an institution is found guilty of deliberately providing false information.)>>endobj2382 0 obj<</Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/Next 2383 0 R/Parent 2379 0 R/Title(Areas of Operation:)>>endobj2383 0 obj<</Dest[27 0 R/Fit]/Parent 2379 0 R/Prev 2382 0 R/Title(Glossary:)>>endobj2513 0 obj<</Author(Rebecca Castle)/CreationDate(D:20260423091537Z)/Creator(Canva)/Keywords(DAFM92rSvi8,BACotTSnvYA,0)/ModDate(D:20260423091532Z)/Producer(Canva)/Title(ASIC UK Handbook V2.2.1-0426)>>endobjxref
